{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0f827bfff9d23a2c47a63907877cd1e4.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=335 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0f827bfff9d23a2c47a63907877cd1e4.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What if Diablo was a deckbuilder?</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>School of Magic</i> lets you create <strong>a new character every run</strong> and carve through enemies for loot and power. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Leveling is its own deckbuilding system</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At each level one card disappears</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The rest grow stronger</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three new ones are added</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Do you play it safe or push your luck for something bigger? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The result <strong>is a unique skill tree  in every run</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0c5cd505777d6ec46b70255a2b64da8f.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0c5cd505777d6ec46b70255a2b64da8f.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Before each run, you don\u2019t pick a rigid class \u2014 you build one yourself. By assembling a spell deck, you decide which abilities can appear, almost like crafting a personal Magic deck. This freedom adds a whole new layer of metagame strategy to the deckbuilding genre. Every decision shapes not only how you carve through hordes of enemies, but also how you\u2019ll survive the bosses that push your build to its limits.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/b4cc39a193f6ec6217181950acfd16e4.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/b4cc39a193f6ec6217181950acfd16e4.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>School of Magic</i> brings its world to life as you experiment, fail, and try again. Every run unlocks new cards and new story fragments, so even defeat pushes the tale forward. With endless combinations and broken builds waiting to be discovered, no two runs will ever feel the same.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1384550?t=1760603580","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1384550?t=1760603580","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/dda06620320d1030fb0052144d301c011ad08413/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1760603580","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/dda06620320d1030fb0052144d301c011ad08413/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1760603580","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0f827bfff9d23a2c47a63907877cd1e4.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=335 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0f827bfff9d23a2c47a63907877cd1e4.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>What if Diablo was a deckbuilder?</strong></h2><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" > </h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>School of Magic</i> lets you create <strong>a new character every run</strong> and carve through enemies for loot and power. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Leveling is its own deckbuilding system</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At each level one card disappears</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The rest grow stronger</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Three new ones are added</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Do you play it safe or push your luck for something bigger? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The result <strong>is a unique skill tree  in every run</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0c5cd505777d6ec46b70255a2b64da8f.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/0c5cd505777d6ec46b70255a2b64da8f.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Before each run, you don\u2019t pick a rigid class \u2014 you build one yourself. By assembling a spell deck, you decide which abilities can appear, almost like crafting a personal Magic deck. This freedom adds a whole new layer of metagame strategy to the deckbuilding genre. Every decision shapes not only how you carve through hordes of enemies, but also how you\u2019ll survive the bosses that push your build to its limits.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/b4cc39a193f6ec6217181950acfd16e4.poster.avif?t=1760603580\" width=800 height=450 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/extras/b4cc39a193f6ec6217181950acfd16e4.webm?t=1760603580\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>School of Magic</i> brings its world to life as you experiment, fail, and try again. Every run unlocks new cards and new story fragments, so even defeat pushes the tale forward. With endless combinations and broken builds waiting to be discovered, no two runs will ever feel the same.</p>","developers":["PartTimeIndie"],"genres":[{"description":"RPG","id":"3"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"},{"description":"Free To Play","id":"37"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1384550/ad4cf61d30f9c494372be7f58f3d349cfe247283/header.jpg?t=1760603580","is_free":true,"legal_notice":"This game collects the following Data: When you start and stop playing the game, which cards you pick, which dialog options you pick when you die, your country, and the version of the game. I use the data to improve the game and it is shared only with unity. If you have any questions you can contact me at <a href=\"mailto:parttimeindie@gmail.com\">parttimeindie@gmail.com</a>.<br>Link to the full pr